cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RWM reproduction: an independent reproduction of the Robotic World Model proprioceptive dynamics model"
message: "If you refer to this reproduction or its findings, please cite it, and cite the original work it reproduces."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Singh
    given-names: Joyjeet
repository-code: "https://github.com/joyjeet-singh/rwm"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - world models
  - model-based reinforcement learning
  - legged robotics
abstract: >-
  An independent CPU reproduction of the proprioceptive dynamics model from
  Robotic World Model (arXiv:2501.10100), verified against the released
  reference at the level of outputs, losses and gradients. Every claim is
  recorded in an append-only findings ledger with an evidence class and a
  source. Principal findings: the released data contains ten episode
  boundaries that its own termination column does not mark, so the released
  window builder trains on 352 spliced windows; the reference's training and
  evaluation code disagree on action alignment and the evaluation side is
  stale by one step, understating the released checkpoint; and the predicted
  variance head collapses because that is the optimum of the released
  objective rather than a training accident.
